      persistence: [78, 0.62, "d", "A"],
      // [src_knuth_chm, src_knuth_stanfordmag, src_knuth_quanta, src_knuth_electronicdesign, src_knuth_stanfordeng | 1977-1993 | museum + alumni magazine + science magazine + trade profile + university page] The Computer History Museum, Stanford Magazine, Quanta and Electronic Design all describe him responding to the poor typography of his own books by building TeX and METAFONT over about a decade, which Stanford Magazine notes he did with limited typesetting experience, by taking design lessons and working with typographers, and then releasing them for free use; Quanta describes his later decision to take leave in 1990 and retire in 1993 to finish the series (Stanford's engineering school and Electronic Design confirm the 1993 retirement). Two documented self-started projects, each told by several independent outlets, so documented at a moderate confidence.
