      // [src_ive_guardian, src_ive_designmuseum, src_ive_newyorker, src_ive_dezeen_ferrari | 1989-2026 | newspaper profile + museum + long-form profile + design press] At the Tangerine consultancy he worked on projects from bathroom ceramics to power tools and televisions (Guardian, Design Museum), and Tangerine's chief executive says he can work on anything; at Apple, Parker reports his remit running through Human Interface (typefaces, icons, sounds), the staircases, signage and precast 'void slabs' of the Apple Park campus, and occasional outside pieces such as a box for a fashion designer's book; Dezeen (2026), relaying Ferrari, reports that after Apple his studio LoveFrom designed the interior and interfaces of the Ferrari Luce. All the work is design, so this is range across product types and scales rather than across unrelated fields, and the later items rest on company statements, hence strong inference at a moderate confidence.
