      competitiveness: [82, 0.64, "d", "D"],
      // [src_kobe_espn_jackson, src_kobe_hof, src_kobe_espn_macmullan, src_kobe_nba_redeem | 1996-2008 | coach's book excerpt + Hall of Fame + long-form feature + league-site feature] Jackson writes that Bryant told teammates he was shooting for ten championships and was hell-bent on surpassing Jordan, and that he asked Jerry West how West had averaged 30 points a game alongside Elgin Baylor; the Hall of Fame credits his work ethic and never-give-an-inch mindset; MacMullan says that by 14 he had decided his quest for greatness would be a solitary journey; NBA.com says he joined the 2008 US team after reportedly telling Carmelo Anthony he was tired of watching them lose. The goals are documented independently of results (he won five titles, not ten). Held at 82 because the key statements come from Jackson's retelling and the 'tired of watching y'all lose' line is reported as alleged.
      achievement_drive: [82, 0.66, "d", "A"],
