      persistence: [70, 0.56, "s", "A"],
      // [src_kobe_espn_jackson, src_kobe_nba_redeem, src_kobe_si_recruit, src_kobe_espn_markazi | 2000-2014 | coach's book excerpt + league-site feature + documentary recap + teammate quotations] Jackson says that when he suggested Bryant might be captain at twenty-five, Bryant replied that he wanted it 'tomorrow', and Jackson answered that a captain needs followers; at the 2008 Olympics NBA.com says he set a tone by defending and diving for 50/50 balls, and Krzyzewski says Bryant chose defence to show the others he was all-in; in 2014 the reporter and teammates describe him taking on a mentor's role, and Jeremy Lin says he has never played with a better leader and mentor. The drive to lead is documented from 2000, but the same sources show it outran his teammates' trust early on, so the impact is dual-edged and the evidence is strong inference.
