      conflict_tolerance: [78, 0.6, "s", "D"],
      // [src_kobe_espn_jackson, src_kobe_espn_macmullan, src_kobe_espn_markazi, src_kobe_si_recruit, src_kobe_ap_2004 | 2000-2014 | coach's book excerpt + long-form feature + teammate quotations + documentary recap + wire report] Jackson says Bryant was a stubborn learner who had to experience failure before an aha moment, and that in early 2000 he began to fit himself into the triangle system; in 2009 he sought out Olajuwon to add post moves; at the 2008 Olympics Krzyzewski says he chose defence to show he was all-in; and in 2014 he described a 'more nurturing' style for a younger team, which Scott and teammates confirm. Documented changes of method across fifteen years, but Jackson's account of his resistance and the 2004 diary suggest he often changed only after conflict, so the score is moderate and dual-edged.
